#!/bin/bash

### This script is called after the user changes environment variables in the
### application setting page.
###
### Deliberately a no-op: cmd/main reads its environment at process start, and
### an implicit stop/start here would tear down the Node host (and any resident
### engine connection / in-flight chat) from inside a settings callback. The
### settings page already tells the user to restart the app for changes to take
### effect. Once fnOS's config-callback semantics and env propagation are
### verified on a real machine, a guarded restart can be added here — do NOT
### add one speculatively.

exit 0
